IMPORT prelude

-- Discrimination Act 1991 (ACT) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR), not the
-- daydate library.
--
-- (c) Australian Capital Territory. Used under CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). Unofficial text.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Discrimination Act 1991`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- Whether the first day is strictly before the second.
GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first` `falls before` `the second` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second`

-- Whether the first day is on or after the second.
GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first` `is on or after` `the second` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first` AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL `the second`

-- Whether a year is a leap year (Gregorian rule).
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a leap year` y IF
        y MODULO 4 EQUALS 0
    AND (    (NOT (y MODULO 100 EQUALS 0))
         OR  y MODULO 400 EQUALS 0)

-- The same day n years later. A 29 February with no 29 February n years later becomes 28 February (the last day of
-- that month; Legislation Act 2001 (ACT) s 151 is not deposited: NOTES.md, fork F10).
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `plus years` n MEANS
    IF      DATE_DAY `the day` EQUALS 29
        AND DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 2
        AND (NOT (`is a leap year` (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS n)))
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS n)
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY (DATE_DAY `the day`) (DATE_MONTH `the day`) (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS n)
